{
    "background_story": "Peach was a free-spirited artist who called Anaheim home. She grew up surrounded by the vibrant city's eclectic mix of cultures and landscapes, which inspired her colorful and whimsical art. Peach spent most of her days exploring the city's hidden gems, from the tranquil Anaheim Packing District to the bustling streets of Little Saigon. Her art studio, tucked away in a converted warehouse, became a hub for local creatives and musicians. Peach's murals, which adorned the city's walls, reflected her love for Anaheim's diversity and resilience. As the city's unofficial ambassador of art, Peach brought people together through her work, celebrating the beauty and uniqueness of Anaheim's community.",
